    "case_summary": "A 13-year-old male with no previous medical history experienced a generalized tonic-clonic seizure in December 2004 following a basketball game. Blood glucose was measured at 33 mg/dL. A second seizure occurred in late January 2005, with a recorded glucose level below 40 mg/dL. During this episode, the C-peptide level was found to be 8.1 U/dL.\n\nHis glucose was 33 mg/dL with an insulin level equal to 21 U/dL. CT scanning and MRI demonstrated a 1.8 cm mass in the neck of the pancreas.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n",
